$.#293
|  Consider red box, and
|  (for sake of argument, although this deviates from the
|  specifics of <!!Gardenfors!!>-inspired work on conceptualization)
|  define the concepts set-theoretically:
|  red means the set of red things; box means the set of
.  boxes (or box-like things)
sdi-sentence-text $# 293 ;.

sdi-new-sentence 4# 293 ;.
sdi-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 293 53001 974 28 ;.
sdi-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 293 53070 975 37 ;.
sdi-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#294
|  Combining the concepts yields
.  an intersection between the two sets
sdi-sentence-text $# 294 ;.

sdi-new-sentence 4# 294 ;.
